From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:35:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Write knulli.conf, es_settings.cfg and gamelists atomically

saveSystemConf wrote knulli.conf.tmp and then copied it over knulli.conf,
truncating it first; es_settings.cfg and gamelist.xml were rewritten in
place by pugixml, and the per-game recovery files were deleted before
being written again. A power cut or hard reboot at the wrong moment left
an empty or partial file, and knulli.conf holds every system setting.

Add Utils::FileSystem::writeFileAtomic: temporary file in the same folder
(mkstemp), same mode and owner as the file it replaces, fsync, rename,
then fsync of the folder; a symlink keeps pointing to the new file. Use
it for knulli.conf, es_settings.cfg, gamelist.xml and the recovery files.

knulli-settings-set also rewrites knulli.conf, under an flock on
/var/run/knulli-settings-set.lock. On Knulli, saveSystemConf now holds
the same lock from reading the file to replacing it (waiting at most
2 s), so neither writer drops the other's change.
---
 es-app/src/Gamelist.cpp              | 17 ++++--
 es-core/src/Settings.cpp             |  6 +-
 es-core/src/SystemConf.cpp           | 60 ++++++++++++++----
 es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.h   |  3 +
 5 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

